  "discovery/confluence/.adapter.md": "# Confluence adapter\n\nThe Confluence adapter exposes spaces and pages under `/confluence`, with writeback routes for creating, updating, and deleting pages.\n\nRead-only mounts:\n- `/confluence/spaces/<spaceIdOrKey>.json` - Space records.\n- `/confluence/pages/<pageId>.json` - Flat page records.\n- `/confluence/spaces/<spaceIdOrKey>/pages/<pageId>.json` - Space-scoped page records.\n\nResources:\n\n| Resource | Schema | Create example | ID pattern | What it does |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `/confluence/pages/<id>.json` | `/confluence/pages/.schema.json` | `/confluence/pages/.create.example.json` | `^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.~-]+(?:--\\|__))?\\d+$` | Creates a Confluence page when `spaceId` is supplied in the document. |\n| `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/<id>.json` | `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/.schema.json` | `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/.create.example.json` | `^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.~-]+(?:--\\|__))?\\d+$` | Creates a Confluence page in the space named by the path. |\n\n## Operations\n\n| To... | Do... |\n|---|---|\n| Read | `cat <canonical-resource-path>` after listing the resource directory or following an alias when one is available. Use the resource table and ID patterns below to determine whether a resource uses a bare id, an adapter-specific slug/id filename, or an exact sidecar path such as `content.md`. |\n| Edit | Write the resource update payload to the canonical resource path. For JSON resources, included mutable fields PATCH; fields marked `readOnly` in `.schema.json` are rejected. |\n| Create | Write JSON to any non-canonical filename such as `create request.json`. The adapter creates the record at its canonical resource path and rewrites the draft as `{ \"created\": \"<real-id>\", \"path\": \"<canonical-resource-path>\", \"url\": \"<provider-url>\" }`. |\n| Ignore | Editor scratch files named `partial.json`, `.tmp.json`, `.partial.json`, `*.tmp.json`, or `*.partial.json` are ignored and never treated as create drafts. |\n| Delete | `rm <canonical-resource-path>` for canonical records. |\n\n## ID Patterns\n- `/confluence/pages/<id>.json`: `^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.~-]+(?:--|__))?\\d+$`. Filenames that do not match this pattern are treated as create drafts.\n- `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/<id>.json`: `^(?:[A-Za-z0-9_.~-]+(?:--|__))?\\d+$`. Filenames that do not match this pattern are treated as create drafts.\n\n## Write field contracts\n\n### Create Confluence page\n\nResource: `/confluence/pages/<id>.json`\nSchema: `/confluence/pages/.schema.json`\nCreate example: `/confluence/pages/.create.example.json`\nRequired fields: `title`, `spaceId`, `body`.\nOptional fields: `status`, `parentId`, `version`.\n\nFields:\n\n- `title` (required, string) - Page title.\n- `spaceId` (required, string) - Confluence space id.\n- `status` (optional, enum) - Page status. Defaults to current. Allowed values: `current`, `draft`.\n- `parentId` (optional, string) - Optional parent page id.\n- `body` (required, one of string, object) - Confluence page body as a storage-format string or a body object with `value`/`representation` or `storage.value`.\n- `version` (optional, object) - Optional synced version object. Updates increment `version.number` when present.\n- `version.number` (optional, integer) - Current Confluence version number.\n- `version.message` (optional, string) - Version message.\n- `version.minorEdit` (optional, boolean) - Whether the update is a minor edit.\n\n### Create Confluence space page\n\nResource: `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/<id>.json`\nSchema: `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/.schema.json`\nCreate example: `/confluence/spaces/{spaceIdOrKey}/pages/.create.example.json`\nRequired fields: `title`, `body`.\nOptional fields: `status`, `parentId`, `version`.\n\nFields:\n\n- `title` (required, string) - Page title.\n- `status` (optional, enum) - Page status. Defaults to current. Allowed values: `current`, `draft`.\n- `parentId` (optional, string) - Optional parent page id.\n- `body` (required, one of string, object) - Confluence page body as a storage-format string or a body object with `value`/`representation` or `storage.value`.\n- `version` (optional, object) - Optional synced version object. Updates increment `version.number` when present.\n- `version.number` (optional, integer) - Current Confluence version number.\n- `version.message` (optional, string) - Version message.\n- `version.minorEdit` (optional, boolean) - Whether the update is a minor edit.\n\n## Create Examples\nRead the resource `.schema.json` first, then use the sibling `.create.example.json` as a minimal create document. The example intentionally omits read-only fields.\n",
